# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Configuration {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper module [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), which the Setup cell downloads, implements the learner. The tutorial calls the following functions from it:\n"
msgstr "Le module d'aide [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), que la cellule de configuration télécharge, implémente l'apprenant. Le tutoriel en appelle les fonctions suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Purpose |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exact MPO of the ideal kicked-Ising state, or of the state after local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Randomly assign measurement settings to training and testing sets (half each by default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow estimates of every learning window, from the training settings only |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior for common randomized measurements (CRM), fitted to the measured purity of each window, as in the paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Sweep the one-site update of the paper along the chain, starting from the maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exact $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ between two MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC estimates of $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ from the testing settings, with jackknife error bars |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Fonction | Rôle |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | MPO exact de l'état d'Ising à impulsions idéal, ou de l'état après un bruit dépolarisant local |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Répartit aléatoirement les réglages de mesure entre ensembles d'entraînement et de test (moitié-moitié par défaut) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Estimations par ombres de chaque fenêtre d'apprentissage, à partir des seuls réglages d'entraînement |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | A priori pour les mesures aléatoires communes (CRM), ajusté à la pureté mesurée de chaque fenêtre, comme dans l'article |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Balaie la chaîne avec la mise à jour à un site de l'article, en partant de l'état maximalement mixte |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ exact et $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ entre deux MPO |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | Estimations AFC de $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ et de $S_2$ à partir des réglages de test, avec barres d'erreur par jackknife |\n"

